;; E, the Roots of the Hum. A's shaft (columns 3-5) comes down onto the
;; low floor; the rough pillar at column 6 hangs to two rows above it, the
;; climb back to A. Cut steps lead east to F (rows 7-8). Two cells of the
;; step (10-11) are false (+): walk onto them and drop into the drip's cell.
(room
  region: underhum
  at: (4 5)
  title: "The Roots of the Hum"
  intent: "at the bottom of the throat, steps cut by the old people lead east: a breath"
  bed: (hum 0.7 air 0.3 water 0.5)
  light: 0.2
  grid:
  ("###   %##################"
   "###   %##################"
   "###   %##################"
   "###   %###  ###   #######"
   "#     %#     #     ######"
   "#     %              ####"
   "#     %                ##"
   "#                        "
   "#                        "
   "#        #++#############"
   "#########################")
  things: ((mural at: (10 9) image: drip-ring))
  decor: none)
